PATCH 328: the flight-model BEARING/RANGE (vertex-emit) chain -- FUN_0000_0541's si/di pointer TRUNCATION
(the crash root), plus the coordinated recovery of the dropped CX/DX/BX register outputs and the int*N
pointer-scaling / 16-bit-width artifacts through 0731 / 0927 / 0b71 / 0baf and the four DGROUP:0x9810
animation methods ab91 / abb7 / abde / ac09.

THE CRASH (exact chain, FIST_SEGV_EBP + nm/addr2line on the default `make native` AZER1 ACCEPT run):
  459a -> c0ca -> c0e5 -> 7c1d -> ab03 -> ab88 -> ab91 -> 0541 -> 0731, SIGSEGV fault-addr ~0x3e09 /
  0x40b9 / 0x42d9 / 0x4a09 in FUN_0000_0731 (+0x15), ~2-5/15 ACCEPT runs (layout-flaky).
ROOT CAUSE: `undefined2` is `uint16_t` (re_out/ghidra_compat.h:30).  Ghidra typed FUN_0000_0541's SI/DI
params from their 16-bit register varnodes as `undefined2`, so the object POINTER its callers pass
(ab88/patch 282 passes g_mem+0x1c000+di; ab91 then passes obj+4 / obj+0x49) was TRUNCATED TO ITS LOW 16
BITS at the call boundary.  FUN_0000_0731 -- whose own params are `uint *` (32-bit) -- then dereferenced
that 16-bit stub as a host address: the observed fault addrs are exactly low16(obj)+0x49+0xc, i.e. the
truncated `di` plus 0731's (mis-scaled) 4th word read.  Nothing else in the chain truncates: 0927's si/di
are `int` and 0b71's are `uint *`, both 32-bit.  This is why the fault address is layout-dependent (it is
low16 of a g_mem address) and why the crash is flaky rather than deterministic.

FIXES (each asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin; DS=SS=DGROUP=0x1c00; CS=0):

(a) FUN_0000_0541 (asm 0x541-0x54b) -- si/di widened from `undefined2` to the 32-bit pointer the asm's
    SI/DI carry (THE crash fix), and 0541's dropped CX/DX outputs published: asm `call 0x731` (AX=bearing),
    `push ax; call 0x927` (dx:ax=range), `mov cx,ax`, `pop ax` => OUT: AX=bearing, CX=range_lo, DX=range_hi.
    The __allregs model returns AX only, so CX/DX were lost.

(b) FUN_0000_0731 (asm 0x731-0x748) -- int*N POINTER-SCALING: the point struct is four 16-bit WORDS (two
    32-bit coords at +0 and +4) and the asm reads [di]/[di+2]/[di+4]/[di+6], but Ghidra typed the pointers
    `uint *` and indexed [1]/[2]/[3] = +4/+8/+12.  Also emitted a bare `return;` from a non-void function
    (the 077e tail-call's AX survived only by codegen accident) -> made explicit.

(c) FUN_0000_0b71 (asm 0xb71-0xbae) -- returns the 48-bit squared delta in AX:DX:CX plus the accumulator
    word selector in BX; the model threads AX only, so Ghidra dropped dx/cx/bx (both non-AX exits
    degenerated to `return 0`).  Same `uint *` +4-vs-+2 scaling as 0731.  Reconstructed 1:1; dx/cx/bx
    published for 0927.

(d) FUN_0000_0927 (asm 0x927-0x9d5) -- reconstructed 1:1.  Because 0b71's dx/cx/bx were dropped, Ghidra
    bound them to 0927's own DEAD INPUT registers (param_2/param_1/param_3), i.e. it stored the CALLER's
    stale cx/dx into the DGROUP:0x2034 accumulator and used a stale bx as the accumulator offset; it also
    fused the two independent `add bx,0x2034` bases into one `int *` walk (piVar7 + 0x101a = +0x4068
    bytes) and lost the 4th accumulator word.  0927's own DX output (the range HIGH word) is published.

(e) FUN_0000_0baf (asm 0xbaf-0xc30) -- the integer square root under (d).  Ghidra rendered the whole
    routine over 32-bit C `int`/`uint`, so every `shl ax,1`/`rcl dx,1` carry became a bit-31 test
    (`param_1 < 0`) where the asm tests bit 15 of a 16-bit register, and the bits shifted out of ax/dx
    never reached the remainder -> a wrong root for every radicand.  Reconstructed at the asm's 16-bit
    widths.  Both exits provably return DX=0 (asm 0xbf8 `mov ax,bp; mov dx,cx` with cx==0 at both loop
    exits; 0xc2d `pop dx` restoring the 0 input) -- which is what 0927's 0x989/0x9a5 paths rely on.

(f) FUN_0000_ab88 (asm 0xab88-0xab90) -- the DGROUP:0x9810 dispatch (image 0x25810) =
    {ab91,abb7,ac09,abde,ac5d,ac72,ac73,ac74,ad11,ad28,ad2a,ad29,ad2b,ad2c,ad2d,ad2e}.  Patch 282's
    arg-less `(*code)(0,0,0,obj)` put the object in slot 4 -- right for ab91/abb7 (di==param_4) but WRONG
    for ac09/abde, whose __allregs varnode order puts di in param_3 (they ran with obj=0).  None of the
    16 targets has a direct caller, so each is now dispatched with its own signature; DI is the only live
    input in all of them (cx/dx/bx are dead on entry -- every use is an output of their own 0541 call).

(g) FUN_0000_ad08 (asm 0xad08-0xad10) + FUN_0000_ad11 (asm 0xad11-0xad27) -- ab88's twin table
    DGROUP:0x9820 (image 0x25820) = {ad11,ad28,ad2a,ad29,ad2b,ad2c,ad2d,ad2e}: patch 285's
    `(*code)(0,0,0,obj)` has the identical slot defect (ad11 takes di as param_1 -> it ran with 0 and
    faulted on `test WORD [di+0x40],2`, fault-addr 0x40); ad28..ad2e are `c3` ret-stubs, so one arg is
    exact.  ad11 is the SOLE READER of the [di+0x53] word (h) restores: its `cmp WORD [di+0x53],0x30` and
    `and WORD [di+0x40],0xfffd` were 4-byte `uint` accesses -- the read pulled [di+0x55]/[di+0x56] in as
    high bits (so the test was essentially never true) and the store clobbered [di+0x42], the animation
    frame counter ab03 increments (patch 246).

(h) FUN_0000_ab91 / abb7 / abde / ac09 (asm 0xab91 / 0xabb7 / 0xabde / 0xac09) -- the RANGE store
    `shl edx,0x8; mov dl,ch; mov WORD [di+0x53],dx`: `shl edx,8` leaves DX = (DL_old << 8) (EDX's high
    half is shifted away and never stored), then `mov dl,ch` fills the low byte, so the stored word is
    ((range_hi & 0xff) << 8) | ((range_lo >> 8) & 0xff) == (uint16_t)(range32 >> 8) -- consumed by ad11
    (`cmp WORD [di+0x53],0x30`).  Ghidra folded that store onto each method's own DEAD INPUT cx/dx, so
    with ab88 passing 0,0 it wrote a constant 0 every tick.  Threaded from 0541's real CX/DX.  Also:
    abde/ac09's `mov bx,WORD [di+0x97]` is a DGROUP NEAR OFFSET read as a 4-byte `int` and used as a host
    pointer (base-loss) -> rebased; their `mov WORD [di+0x53],dx` / `[di+0x30],ax` / `or WORD [di+0x40]`
    were emitted as 4-byte `int` stores (store-width class, clobbering [di+0x55]/[di+0x42]) -> restored to
    the asm widths; and ac09's frame-count limit walk `mov bx,[0x9796]; mov bx,[bx]; cmp al,[bx-0x66b2]`
    (two chained DGROUP near offsets) was a host deref with -0x66b2 scaled by 4 (`int *` arithmetic) ->
    rebased onto DS=DGROUP.

SCOPE / HONESTY:
  - MISSION-PATH ONLY: 0541/0731/0927/0b71/0baf are the in-mission flight/AI bearing+range helpers and
    ab88's 0x9810 methods run only on the 459a in-mission tick -> behaviour-neutral for the 24 menu /
    settings verify flows (verified native 24/24 + wasm 24/24, native<->wasm 0-diff).
  - There is NO mission-cockpit DOSBox pixel reference, so the acceptance bar here is asm-faithfulness +
    crash-freedom + zero regression; the pixel bit-verify defers to when such a reference exists.
  - DOCUMENTED LATENT DEBT (same class, NOT touched -- each needs its own caller-asm verification):
    FUN_0000_0426 / 0539 / 059a forward si/di to 0731 through `undefined2` params and carry the identical
